        "Getter logic for detecting bold numbered lists is fundamentally flawed for Word/LibreOffice document structure",
        "The getter only checks para.runs[0].bold, which assumes the number is in the first run - this fails for auto-numbered lists where numbers are rendered separately from text content",
        "The regex pattern '^\\d+[\\.\\)]' matches paragraph text, but auto-numbered lists in Word/LibreOffice often don't include the number in para.text - it's part of list formatting metadata",
        "The getter cannot distinguish between manual numbered lists (typed '1. text') and auto-numbered lists (Word's numbering feature) which require different bold detection approaches",
        "Edge case handling is problematic: returns 1.0 (full credit) when no numbered items found, which could mask getter failures or documents without numbered lists",
        "Missing validation: No check for whether bold formatting is applied via list style properties (numbering definition) vs. direct character formatting"
      ],
      "llm_judge_fix_suggestions": [
        "Use python-docx's paragraph.style and numbering properties to detect auto-numbered lists, not just regex on paragraph text",
        "Check paragraph._element.pPr.numPr to determine if paragraph is part of a numbered list",
        "For auto-numbered lists, check if the numbering definition includes bold formatting via abstractNum and lvl properties",
        "For manual typed numbers, iterate through all runs to find runs containing number patterns and check their bold property, not just first run",
        "Add proper edge case handling: return 0.0 or error when no numbered items found if instruction explicitly requires them",
        "Consider using paragraph.style.font.bold or checking the numbering level formatting rather than only run-level formatting"
